IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `hbc-contracts`

-- Home Building Contracts Act 1991 (WA) -- the Q&A layer: the questions people ask, with the seat and the situation as
-- parameters.
--
-- PURPOSE. One module whose exported questions serve every seat from one deployment. Every exported question takes
-- `my role` first ("Which of these describes you"). A question about another role answers `does not arise for you`
-- without reading any other input, so the site's question form never asks those inputs and drops the question.
--
-- ROLES. The baseline (hbc-contracts.l4) was written from the seat of the home owner contracting a builder (s 3(1)
-- "owner"). The Act puts its duties on the other party, the builder (ss 4, 5, 7, 8, 10, 13, 14, 25C), so the builder is
-- the second role:
--   - the home owner having home building work done: every baseline question;
--   - the builder doing it: whether the Act covers the contract, what the builder must give the owner and when, what
--     the builder may take or charge, and the home indemnity insurance the builder must have.
-- The Building Commissioner, the State Administrative Tribunal and the insurer are never seats.
--
-- The baseline's `Contract` record speaks as the owner in two of its fields ("is signed by the builder and by me", "I
-- was given the notice before I signed"). It is the one record both roles answer, so its @desc here says that "I" and
-- "me" in its fields mean the owner. The builder's questions read none of those two fields.
--
-- SITUATIONS (design D8 of the Graffiti Vandalism Act encoding). Within a role, a question that arises only in a
-- situation takes that situation's fact straight after `my role`, and answers `does not arise for you` when it does not
-- hold, without reading anything else. The questions of one situation share one input (same name, type and @desc).
--   - `the building work has started` (BOOLEAN): s 10(3), (5), for both roles. FALSE: does not arise.
--   - `the contract is being varied` (BOOLEAN): ss 7, 8, for both roles. FALSE: does not arise.
--   - `the builder wants to raise the price, or has given notice of a rise` (BOOLEAN): s 13 and Schedule 1 cl 4(b), for
--     both roles. FALSE: does not arise.
--   - `the owner ended the contract after a notified price rise (Schedule 1 clause 4(b))` (BOOLEAN): Schedule 1
--     cl 4(c), for both roles. FALSE: does not arise.
--   - `the building permit was not granted within 45 working days` (BOOLEAN): s 9, Schedule 1 cll 1-3, for both roles.
--     FALSE: does not arise.
--   - `a defect in the work has been found` (BOOLEAN): s 11, one question for both roles. FALSE: does not arise.
-- A question that arises in every situation of its role takes no situation input.
--
-- The rules are in hbc-contracts.l4. This module calls them and restates none; for the owner each answer is the
-- baseline export's own answer, wrapped (one exception, the s 8(3) days, NOTES.md). The builder's questions use the
-- baseline's rules, through small helpers that word the builder's enums. No exported question takes a DEONTIC or EVENT
-- input.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md, "Q&A layer (seat and situations as parameters)".

§ `Home Building Contracts Act 1991 (WA) -- the questions people ask`

§§ `Who is asking, and the shape of the answers`

DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `I am the home owner having home building work done`
    `I am the builder doing home building work for an owner`

DECLARE `Yes or no` IS ONE OF
    yes
    no
    `does not arise for you`

DECLARE `Amount` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    amount HAS dollars IS A NUMBER

-- The baseline's day and year counts, wrapped. Where the baseline answers 0 the Act sets no such time for that contract
-- (it is not one the Act covers, or no insurance is required); the wrapped answer keeps the 0.
DECLARE `Working days` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `working days` HAS `number` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Years` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    years HAS `number` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `What happens to the contract` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the answer` IS A `Permit outcome`

-- s 8(1), (2): the builder's statement of reason and cost, and by when.
DECLARE `When my variation statement is due` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `no s 8 statement: s 8 does not apply, so the variation must be in writing and signed by the owner (s 7)`
    `within 10 working days after I received notice of the direction`
    `within 10 working days after I became aware, or should reasonably have become aware, of the circumstances`

-- The builder's words for the baseline's owner-voiced enums.
DECLARE `Who failed, as the builder sees it` IS ONE OF
    `I alone`
    `the owner alone`
    `both of us`
    `neither of us`

DECLARE `Reason for my price rise` IS ONE OF
    `a rise in labour or material costs`
    `a cost imposed directly by a written law`
    `a rise in a tax, duty or charge after the contract date`
    `a start delayed over 45 working days by the owner's failure alone`
    `a start delayed over 45 working days with neither of us at fault`
    `a start delayed over 45 working days by me`

§§ `Helpers`

GIVEN `it holds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`yes if` `it holds` MEANS
    IF `it holds` THEN yes ELSE no

-- These helpers list every value and have no OTHERWISE (graffiti finding 31).
GIVEN `who` IS A `Who failed, as the builder sees it`
GIVETH A `Who failed`
`the owner's words for` `who` MEANS
    CONSIDER `who`
    WHEN `I alone` THEN `the builder alone`
    WHEN `the owner alone` THEN `me alone`
    WHEN `both of us` THEN `both of us`
    WHEN `neither of us` THEN `neither of us`

GIVEN `the reason` IS A `Reason for my price rise`
GIVETH A `Reason for a price rise`
`the owner's words for the reason` `the reason` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the reason`
    WHEN `a rise in labour or material costs` THEN `a rise in labour or material costs`
    WHEN `a cost imposed directly by a written law` THEN `a cost imposed directly by a written law`
    WHEN `a rise in a tax, duty or charge after the contract date` THEN `a rise in a tax, duty or charge after the contract date`
    WHEN `a start delayed over 45 working days by the owner's failure alone` THEN `a start delayed over 45 working days by my failure alone`
    WHEN `a start delayed over 45 working days with neither of us at fault` THEN `a start delayed over 45 working days with neither of us at fault`
    WHEN `a start delayed over 45 working days by me` THEN `a start delayed over 45 working days by the builder`

-- s 8(1), (2): the statement is due "within 10 working days after the builder -- (a) received notice of the direction
-- ...; or (b) became aware, or should reasonably have become aware, of the circumstances". s 8 does not reach an agreed
-- change, and (s 8(4)) not a variation made necessary "by reason only of an increase in the costs of labour ... or
-- materials": those must be in writing and signed under s 7.
GIVEN `the cause` IS A `Cause of the variation`
GIVETH A `When my variation statement is due`
`the s 8 statement time for` `the cause` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the cause`
    WHEN `a change we agreed` THEN `no s 8 statement: s 8 does not apply, so the variation must be in writing and signed by the owner (s 7)`
    WHEN `a written direction under a written law` THEN `within 10 working days after I received notice of the direction`
    WHEN `circumstances the builder could not reasonably have foreseen` THEN `within 10 working days after I became aware, or should reasonably have become aware, of the circumstances`
    WHEN `a rise in the builder's labour or material costs` THEN `no s 8 statement: s 8 does not apply, so the variation must be in writing and signed by the owner (s 7)`

§§ `For the home owner`

§§§ `ss 3, 4, 5 -- the work, the contract and the notice`

@export Is my contract one the Home Building Contracts Act covers -- a home building work contract (Home Building Contracts Act 1991 (WA) s 3; r 2A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the contract` IS A Contract @desc The home building contract between the owner and the builder (where a field says "I" or "me", it means the owner)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does the Act cover my contract as the owner` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the home owner having home building work done` THEN `yes if` (`Is my contract a home building work contract` `the contract`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is my contract made the way the Act requires -- in writing, dated, and signed by both of us (Home Building Contracts Act 1991 (WA) s 4(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the contract` IS A Contract @desc The home building contract between the owner and the builder (where a field says "I" or "me", it means the owner)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my contract made the way the Act requires` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the home owner having home building work done` THEN `yes if` (`Is my contract made as the Act requires` `the contract`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must I be given the Notice for the Home Owner before I sign (Home Building Contracts Act 1991 (WA) s 4(3); r 3)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the contract` IS A Contract @desc The home building contract between the owner and the builder (where a field says "I" or "me", it means the owner)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I be given the Notice for the Home Owner before I sign` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the home owner having home building work done` THEN `yes if` (`Must I be given the notice before I sign` `the contract`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Within how many working days of my written request must the builder give me a copy of the contract (Home Building Contracts Act 1991 (WA) s 5(3); 0 if the Act does not cover the contract)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the contract` IS A Contract @desc The home building contract between the owner and the builder (where a field says "I" or "me", it means the owner)
GIVETH A `Working days`
`Within how many working days must the builder give me a copy of the contract` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the home owner having home building work done` THEN `working days` (`Within how many working days must the builder give me a copy` `the contract`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 10 -- deposit and progress payments`

@export What is the most deposit my builder may take before work starts, in dollars (Home Building Contracts Act 1991 (WA) s 10(1)(a); r 3A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the contract` IS A Contract @desc The home building contract between the owner and the builder (where a field says "I" or "me", it means the owner)
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most deposit my builder may take before work starts` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the home owner having home building work done` THEN amount (`What is the most deposit my builder may take` `the contract`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Do my contract's payment terms break the Act's limits on deposits and progress payments (Home Building Contracts Act 1991 (WA) s 10(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the contract` IS A Contract @desc The home building contract between the owner and the builder (where a field says "I" or "me", it means the owner)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Do the payment terms of my contract break the limits` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the home owner having home building work done` THEN `yes if` (`Do my contract's payment terms break the limits` `the contract`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Once work has started, may my builder demand this payment from me (Home Building Contracts Act 1991 (WA) s 10(3), (5))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the building work has started` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home building work under the contract has started
      `the contract` IS A Contract @desc The home building contract between the owner and the builder (where a field says "I" or "me", it means the owner)
      `it is for work already done or materials already supplied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment for work already done, or materials or services already supplied?
      `it follows the contract's schedule of stage payments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment demanded in accordance with a schedule of stage payments in the contract?
      `it has been shown not to be for work done` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it been shown (for example on a complaint) that the payment is not for work done or materials supplied?
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Once work has started may my builder demand this payment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the home owner having home building work done` THEN
        IF `the building work has started`
        THEN `yes if` (`May my builder demand this progress payment` `the contract` `it is for work already done or materials already supplied` `it follows the contract's schedule of stage payments` `it has been shown not to be for work done`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 4(5), 10(4), 14, 19 -- ending the contract for the way it was made`

@export Is my cost plus contract missing the heading and acknowledgment the Act requires (Home Building Contracts Act 1991 (WA) s 14(1), (2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the contract` IS A Contract @desc The home building contract between the owner and the builder (where a field says "I" or "me", it means the owner)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my cost plus contract missing the heading or acknowledgment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the home owner having home building work done` THEN `yes if` (`Is my cost plus contract missing its heading or acknowledgment` `the contract`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May I end my contract because of the way it was made, by a signed written notice to the builder (Home Building Contracts Act 1991 (WA) ss 4(5), 10(4), 14(3), 19)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the contract` IS A Contract @desc The home building contract between the owner and the builder (where a field says "I" or "me", it means the owner)
      `the work is complete` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the home building work under the contract been completed?
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I end my contract for the way it was made` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the home owner having home building work done` THEN `yes if` (`May I terminate my contract for the way it was made` `the contract` `the work is complete`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 7, 8 -- variations`

@export Must this variation be put in writing, with its cost, dated and signed by me before it binds me (Home Building Contracts Act 1991 (WA) ss 7(1), 8)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the contract is being varied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the contract is being, or has been, varied (a change to the work, the price or other terms after the contract was made)
      `the contract` IS A Contract @desc The home building contract between the owner and the builder (where a field says "I" or "me", it means the owner)
      `the cause` IS A `Cause of the variation` @desc What made the variation necessary (or what the builder says made it necessary)
      `working days until the builder's statement` IS A NUMBER @desc Working days after the builder got the direction or learned of the circumstances that the builder gave the owner a written statement of reason and cost; -1 if none
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must this variation be in writing and signed by me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the home owner having home building work done` THEN
        IF `the contract is being varied`
        THEN `yes if` (`Must the variation be in writing and signed by me` `the contract` `the cause` `working days until the builder's statement`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Was my variation made as the Act requires -- written with its terms and cost, dated, signed by both of us, and a copy given to me before the work on it began (Home Building Contracts Act 1991 (WA) s 7(1), (2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the contract is being varied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the contract is being, or has been, varied (a change to the work, the price or other terms after the contract was made)
      `in writing with its terms and cost` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the variation in writing, setting out all its terms and its cost?
      `dated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it show the date of the variation?
      `signed by both of us` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it signed by the builder and by the owner (or their agents)?
      `copy given before the varied work began` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the owner given a copy of the signed variation before the work it covers began?
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Was my variation made the way the Act requires` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the home owner having home building work done` THEN
        IF `the contract is being varied`
        THEN `yes if` (`Was my variation made as the Act requires` `in writing with its terms and cost` `dated` `signed by both of us` `copy given before the varied work began`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- s 8(3) arises only on the builder's statement of unforeseen circumstances. For the other causes the baseline answers
-- 0, meaning there is no such time; here they answer `does not arise for you` (NOTES.md, decisions).
@export If I think the builder's "unforeseen circumstances" are not unforeseen, within how many working days of the statement must I complain (Home Building Contracts Act 1991 (WA) s 8(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the contract is being varied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the contract is being, or has been, varied (a change to the work, the price or other terms after the contract was made)
      `the cause` IS A `Cause of the variation` @desc What made the variation necessary (or what the builder says made it necessary)
GIVETH A `Working days`
`Within how many working days must I dispute the builder's unforeseen circumstances` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the home owner having home building work done` THEN
        IF `the contract is being varied`
        THEN CONSIDER `the cause`
             WHEN `circumstances the builder could not reasonably have foreseen` THEN `working days` (`Within how many working days must I dispute an unforeseen variation` `the cause`)
             WHEN `a change we agreed` THEN `does not arise for you`
             WHEN `a written direction under a written law` THEN `does not arise for you`
             WHEN `a rise in the builder's labour or material costs` THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 13 and Schedule 1 cl 4 -- the fixed price and price rises`

@export Can my builder put my price up for this reason (Home Building Contracts Act 1991 (WA) s 13)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the builder wants to raise the price, or has given notice of a rise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the builder wants to raise the contract price, or has given the owner notice of a price rise
      `the contract` IS A Contract @desc The home building contract between the owner and the builder (where a field says "I" or "me", it means the owner)
      `the reason` IS A `Reason for a price rise` @desc Why the builder wants to raise the price
      `my contract has a clause allowing it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the contract contain a clause allowing a rise for that reason?
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can my builder put my price up for this reason` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the home owner having home building work done` THEN
        IF `the builder wants to raise the price, or has given notice of a rise`
        THEN `yes if` (`Can my builder raise my price` `the contract` `the reason` `my contract has a clause allowing it`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export After a notified price rise for a delayed start or a late permit, may I end the contract (Home Building Contracts Act 1991 (WA) Schedule 1 cl 4(b))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the builder wants to raise the price, or has given notice of a rise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the builder wants to raise the contract price, or has given the owner notice of a price rise
      `the contract` IS A Contract @desc The home building contract between the owner and the builder (where a field says "I" or "me", it means the owner)
      `the increase` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of the price increase in the builder's notice
      `working days since I received the notice` IS A NUMBER @desc Working days since the owner received the builder's written notice of the increase
      `the work is complete` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the home building work under the contract been completed?
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`After a notified price rise may I end the contract` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the home owner having home building work done` THEN
        IF `the builder wants to raise the price, or has given notice of a rise`
        THEN `yes if` (`May I terminate because of the price rise` `the contract` `the increase` `working days since I received the notice` `the work is complete`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export If I end the contract over a price rise, must I pay the builder's reasonable costs up to then (Home Building Contracts Act 1991 (WA) Schedule 1 cl 4(c))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the owner ended the contract after a notified price rise (Schedule 1 clause 4(b))` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the owner has ended the contract under Schedule 1 clause 4(b), after the builder's notice of a price rise of more than 5%
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`If I end the contract over a price rise must I pay the builder's reasonable costs` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the home owner having home building work done` THEN
        IF `the owner ended the contract after a notified price rise (Schedule 1 clause 4(b))`
        THEN `yes if` (`Must I pay the builder's reasonable costs` `the owner ended the contract after a notified price rise (Schedule 1 clause 4(b))`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 9 and Schedule 1 cll 1-3 -- the building permit condition`

@export If the building permit is not granted within 45 working days, what happens to my contract (Home Building Contracts Act 1991 (WA) s 9; Schedule 1 cll 1-3)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the building permit was not granted within 45 working days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the building permit (or the Water Services Act clearance) was not granted within 45 working days from the date of the contract
      `the contract` IS A Contract @desc The home building contract between the owner and the builder (where a field says "I" or "me", it means the owner)
      `who failed` IS A `Who failed` @desc Whose failure to do what s 9(2) required meant the permit was not granted in time
GIVETH A `What happens to the contract`
`If the permit is late what happens to my contract` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the home owner having home building work done` THEN
        IF `the building permit was not granted within 45 working days`
        THEN `the answer is` (`What happens if the permit is late` `the contract` `who failed`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 26, 28 -- inspection and no contracting out`

@export Is this restriction on my inspecting the work binding on me (Home Building Contracts Act 1991 (WA) s 26(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the restriction` IS AN `Inspection restriction` @desc What your contract says about inspecting the work
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is this restriction on my inspecting the work binding` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the home owner having home building work done` THEN `yes if` (`Is this inspection restriction binding` `the restriction`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Does a term by which I give up a right the Act gives me bind me (Home Building Contracts Act 1991 (WA) s 28)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `it is to my disadvantage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the term exclude, restrict or modify the Act to your disadvantage, or waive a right it gives you?
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does a term giving up my rights bind me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the home owner having home building work done` THEN `yes if` (`Does my waiver bind me` `it is to my disadvantage`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `Part 3A -- home indemnity insurance`

@export What is the "cost of the building work" for home indemnity insurance, in dollars (Home Building Contracts Act 1991 (WA) s 25A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the contract` IS A Contract @desc The home building contract between the owner and the builder (where a field says "I" or "me", it means the owner)
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the cost of the building work for insurance` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the home owner having home building work done` THEN amount (`What is the cost of my building work` `the contract`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is my work "residential building work" for home indemnity insurance (Home Building Contracts Act 1991 (WA) s 25A; r 7)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the contract` IS A Contract @desc The home building contract between the owner and the builder (where a field says "I" or "me", it means the owner)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my work residential building work for insurance` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the home owner having home building work done` THEN `yes if` (`Is my work residential building work` `the contract`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must my builder have home indemnity insurance (or approved-fund cover) for my work (Home Building Contracts Act 1991 (WA) ss 25B, 25C(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the contract` IS A Contract @desc The home building contract between the owner and the builder (where a field says "I" or "me", it means the owner)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must my builder have home indemnity insurance for my work` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the home owner having home building work done` THEN `yes if` (`Must my builder insure my work` `the contract`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must I be given the insurance certificate before the builder asks me for any payment, even the deposit (Home Building Contracts Act 1991 (WA) s 25C(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the contract` IS A Contract @desc The home building contract between the owner and the builder (where a field says "I" or "me", it means the owner)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I be given the insurance certificate before any payment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the home owner having home building work done` THEN `yes if` (`Must I get the insurance certificate before any payment` `the contract`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May my builder ask me for this deposit now (Home Building Contracts Act 1991 (WA) ss 10(1)(a), 25C(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the contract` IS A Contract @desc The home building contract between the owner and the builder (where a field says "I" or "me", it means the owner)
      `the deposit asked` IS A NUMBER @desc The deposit the builder is asking for before work starts
      `I have the insurance certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been given the certificate of home indemnity insurance?
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May my builder ask me for this deposit now` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the home owner having home building work done` THEN `yes if` (`May my builder ask me for this deposit` `the contract` `the deposit asked` `I have the insurance certificate`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export At least how much must the home indemnity insurance cover me for, in dollars (Home Building Contracts Act 1991 (WA) s 25D(1)(e); r 7B; 0 if no insurance is required)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the contract` IS A Contract @desc The home building contract between the owner and the builder (where a field says "I" or "me", it means the owner)
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`At least how much must the insurance cover me for` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the home owner having home building work done` THEN amount (`How much must the insurance cover me for` `the contract`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How much of my deposit is insured if my builder dies, disappears, becomes insolvent or loses registration, in dollars (Home Building Contracts Act 1991 (WA) s 25D(1)(a)(i); r 7A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the contract` IS A Contract @desc The home building contract between the owner and the builder (where a field says "I" or "me", it means the owner)
      `deposit I paid` IS A NUMBER @desc The deposit you paid
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`How much of my deposit is insured if my builder fails` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the home owner having home building work done` THEN amount (`How much of my deposit is insured` `the contract` `deposit I paid`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export For how many years after practical completion can I claim on the home indemnity insurance (Home Building Contracts Act 1991 (WA) s 25D(1)(d); 0 if no insurance is required)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the contract` IS A Contract @desc The home building contract between the owner and the builder (where a field says "I" or "me", it means the owner)
GIVETH A `Years`
`For how many years after practical completion can I claim on the insurance` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the home owner having home building work done` THEN years (`For how many years can I claim on the insurance` `the contract`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most excess the home indemnity policy may make me bear on a claim, in dollars (Home Building Contracts Act 1991 (WA) r 5; 0 if no insurance is required)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the contract` IS A Contract @desc The home building contract between the owner and the builder (where a field says "I" or "me", it means the owner)
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most excess the policy may make me bear` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the home owner having home building work done` THEN amount (`What is the most excess on my claim` `the contract`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `Disputes -- the time limits in the Notice for the Home Owner`

@export Within how many years must I complain to the Building Commissioner (Home Building Contracts Act 1991 (WA) s 17; Notice for the Home Owner, "Disputes")?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the kind` IS A `Kind of complaint` @desc What the complaint is about
GIVETH A `Years`
`Within how many years must I complain to the Building Commissioner` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the home owner having home building work done` THEN years (`Within how many years must I complain` `the kind`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the home owner and the builder`

§§§ `s 11 -- defects`

-- s 11(1): "the builder is liable to make good at the cost of the builder defects in the home building work notified
-- in writing to the builder within the period of 4 months commencing on the day of practical completion". The same
-- answer serves both roles.
@export Must the builder make good this defect at the builder's own cost (Home Building Contracts Act 1991 (WA) s 11)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `a defect in the work has been found` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a defect has been found in the home building work
      `the contract` IS A Contract @desc The home building contract between the owner and the builder (where a field says "I" or "me", it means the owner)
      `months after practical completion it was notified in writing` IS A NUMBER @desc How many whole months after practical completion the defect was notified to the builder in writing (0 = within the first month); -1 if not notified in writing
      `longer period in the contract in months` IS A NUMBER @desc A notification period longer than 4 months given by the contract, in months; 0 if none
      `the contract declares the builder not liable for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the contract specifically declare the builder not liable for this failure?
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must the builder make good this defect` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the home owner having home building work done` THEN
        IF `a defect in the work has been found`
        THEN `yes if` (`Must my builder make good this defect` `the contract` `months after practical completion it was notified in writing` `longer period in the contract in months` `the contract declares the builder not liable for it`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    WHEN `I am the builder doing home building work for an owner` THEN
        IF `a defect in the work has been found`
        THEN `yes if` (`Must my builder make good this defect` `the contract` `months after practical completion it was notified in writing` `longer period in the contract in months` `the contract declares the builder not liable for it`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the builder`

§§§ `ss 3, 4, 5 -- the work, the contract and the notice`

@export Does the Home Building Contracts Act cover my contract with the owner -- is it a home building work contract (Home Building Contracts Act 1991 (WA) s 3; r 2A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the contract` IS A Contract @desc The home building contract between the owner and the builder (where a field says "I" or "me", it means the owner)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does the Act cover my contract as the builder` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the builder doing home building work for an owner` THEN `yes if` (`Is my contract a home building work contract` `the contract`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- s 4(1): "A contract" (a home building work contract, s 3(1)) "must be in writing ... showing the date ... and must be
-- signed by the builder and the owner"; s 4(5): if not, the owner may terminate.
@export Must my contract with the owner be in writing, set out all its terms, show its date and be signed by us both (Home Building Contracts Act 1991 (WA) s 4(1), (5))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the contract` IS A Contract @desc The home building contract between the owner and the builder (where a field says "I" or "me", it means the owner)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must my contract be in writing dated and signed by us both` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the builder doing home building work for an owner` THEN `yes if` (`Is my contract a home building work contract` `the contract`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must I give the owner the Notice for the Home Owner before they sign (Home Building Contracts Act 1991 (WA) s 4(2), (3); r 3)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the contract` IS A Contract @desc The home building contract between the owner and the builder (where a field says "I" or "me", it means the owner)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I give the owner the Notice for the Home Owner` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the builder doing home building work for an owner` THEN `yes if` (`Must I be given the notice before I sign` `the contract`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Within how many working days of the owner's written request must I give them a copy of the contract (Home Building Contracts Act 1991 (WA) s 5(3); 0 if the Act does not cover the contract)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the contract` IS A Contract @desc The home building contract between the owner and the builder (where a field says "I" or "me", it means the owner)
GIVETH A `Working days`
`Within how many working days must I give the owner a copy of the contract` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the builder doing home building work for an owner` THEN `working days` (`Within how many working days must the builder give me a copy` `the contract`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 10 -- deposit and progress payments`

@export What is the most deposit I may take from the owner before work starts, in dollars (Home Building Contracts Act 1991 (WA) s 10(1)(a); r 3A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the contract` IS A Contract @desc The home building contract between the owner and the builder (where a field says "I" or "me", it means the owner)
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most deposit I may take before work starts` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the builder doing home building work for an owner` THEN amount (`What is the most deposit my builder may take` `the contract`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Once work has started, may I demand this payment from the owner (Home Building Contracts Act 1991 (WA) s 10(3), (5))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the building work has started` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home building work under the contract has started
      `the contract` IS A Contract @desc The home building contract between the owner and the builder (where a field says "I" or "me", it means the owner)
      `it is for work already done or materials already supplied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment for work already done, or materials or services already supplied?
      `it follows the contract's schedule of stage payments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the payment demanded in accordance with a schedule of stage payments in the contract?
      `it has been shown not to be for work done` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it been shown (for example on a complaint) that the payment is not for work done or materials supplied?
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Once work has started may I demand this payment from the owner` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the builder doing home building work for an owner` THEN
        IF `the building work has started`
        THEN `yes if` (`May my builder demand this progress payment` `the contract` `it is for work already done or materials already supplied` `it follows the contract's schedule of stage payments` `it has been shown not to be for work done`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 7, 8 -- variations`

@export Must this variation be in writing, with its cost, dated and signed by the owner before it binds them (Home Building Contracts Act 1991 (WA) ss 7(1), 8)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the contract is being varied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the contract is being, or has been, varied (a change to the work, the price or other terms after the contract was made)
      `the contract` IS A Contract @desc The home building contract between the owner and the builder (where a field says "I" or "me", it means the owner)
      `the cause` IS A `Cause of the variation` @desc What made the variation necessary (or what the builder says made it necessary)
      `working days until the builder's statement` IS A NUMBER @desc Working days after the builder got the direction or learned of the circumstances that the builder gave the owner a written statement of reason and cost; -1 if none
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must this variation be in writing and signed by the owner` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the builder doing home building work for an owner` THEN
        IF `the contract is being varied`
        THEN `yes if` (`Must the variation be in writing and signed by me` `the contract` `the cause` `working days until the builder's statement`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export By when must I give the owner my statement of the reason for and cost of a variation, so that it need not be signed by them (Home Building Contracts Act 1991 (WA) s 8(1), (2), (4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the contract is being varied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the contract is being, or has been, varied (a change to the work, the price or other terms after the contract was made)
      `the cause` IS A `Cause of the variation` @desc What made the variation necessary (or what the builder says made it necessary)
GIVETH A `When my variation statement is due`
`By when must I give the owner my variation statement` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the builder doing home building work for an owner` THEN
        IF `the contract is being varied`
        THEN `the s 8 statement time for` `the cause`
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 13 and Schedule 1 cl 4 -- the fixed price and price rises`

@export May I put the owner's price up for this reason (Home Building Contracts Act 1991 (WA) s 13)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the builder wants to raise the price, or has given notice of a rise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the builder wants to raise the contract price, or has given the owner notice of a price rise
      `the contract` IS A Contract @desc The home building contract between the owner and the builder (where a field says "I" or "me", it means the owner)
      `my reason` IS A `Reason for my price rise` @desc Why you want to raise the price
      `my contract has a clause allowing it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the contract contain a clause allowing a rise for that reason?
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I put the owner's price up for this reason` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the builder doing home building work for an owner` THEN
        IF `the builder wants to raise the price, or has given notice of a rise`
        THEN `yes if` (`Can my builder raise my price` `the contract` (`the owner's words for the reason` `my reason`) `my contract has a clause allowing it`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export If the owner ends the contract after my notice of a price rise, must they pay my reasonable costs up to then (Home Building Contracts Act 1991 (WA) Schedule 1 cl 4(c))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the owner ended the contract after a notified price rise (Schedule 1 clause 4(b))` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the owner has ended the contract under Schedule 1 clause 4(b), after the builder's notice of a price rise of more than 5%
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`If the owner ends the contract over my price rise must they pay my reasonable costs` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the builder doing home building work for an owner` THEN
        IF `the owner ended the contract after a notified price rise (Schedule 1 clause 4(b))`
        THEN `yes if` (`Must I pay the builder's reasonable costs` `the owner ended the contract after a notified price rise (Schedule 1 clause 4(b))`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 9 and Schedule 1 cll 1-3 -- the building permit condition`

@export If the building permit is not granted within 45 working days, what happens to my contract with the owner (Home Building Contracts Act 1991 (WA) s 9; Schedule 1 cll 1-3)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the building permit was not granted within 45 working days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the building permit (or the Water Services Act clearance) was not granted within 45 working days from the date of the contract
      `the contract` IS A Contract @desc The home building contract between the owner and the builder (where a field says "I" or "me", it means the owner)
      `who failed, as I see it` IS A `Who failed, as the builder sees it` @desc Whose failure to do what s 9(2) required meant the permit was not granted in time
GIVETH A `What happens to the contract`
`If the permit is late what happens to my contract with the owner` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the builder doing home building work for an owner` THEN
        IF `the building permit was not granted within 45 working days`
        THEN `the answer is` (`What happens if the permit is late` `the contract` (`the owner's words for` `who failed, as I see it`))
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `Part 3A -- home indemnity insurance`

@export Must I have home indemnity insurance (or approved-fund cover) before I do this work (Home Building Contracts Act 1991 (WA) ss 25B, 25C(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the contract` IS A Contract @desc The home building contract between the owner and the builder (where a field says "I" or "me", it means the owner)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I have home indemnity insurance for this work` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the builder doing home building work for an owner` THEN `yes if` (`Must my builder insure my work` `the contract`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must I give the owner the insurance certificate before I demand any payment, even the deposit (Home Building Contracts Act 1991 (WA) s 25C(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the contract` IS A Contract @desc The home building contract between the owner and the builder (where a field says "I" or "me", it means the owner)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I give the owner the insurance certificate before any payment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the builder doing home building work for an owner` THEN `yes if` (`Must I get the insurance certificate before any payment` `the contract`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export At least how much must my home indemnity insurance cover the owner for, in dollars (Home Building Contracts Act 1991 (WA) s 25D(1)(e); r 7B; 0 if no insurance is required)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the contract` IS A Contract @desc The home building contract between the owner and the builder (where a field says "I" or "me", it means the owner)
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`At least how much must my insurance cover the owner for` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the builder doing home building work for an owner` THEN amount (`How much must the insurance cover me for` `the contract`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`
